# Which country has emitted the most CO₂ since 1750?
subtitle: "Rank five countries by all the CO₂ they have ever emitted, then rewind to 1850 to see who started it all, as two hosts argue it out."
tags: ["earth","history","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Not who you'd blame\" note \"All-time CO₂\""

## Which country has emitted the most CO₂ since 1750?
text: {"font_size":34}
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - UK
      - Germany
      - Russia
      - China
      - USA
    values:
      - [4, 5, 7, 15, 24]
      - [78, 5, 0, 0, 4]
    stage: 0
    value_labels: true
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 80
    y_label: '% of all CO₂'
    bar_colors: same
    label_size: 34
    icons:
      - {of: flag united kingdom, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag germany, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag russia, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag china, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag united states, set: twemoji}
sources:
    - id: owid_cum
      title: Cumulative CO₂ emissions
      authors: Our World in Data, from the Global Carbon Budget (2025)
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/cumulative-co-emissions
      finding: 'fossil and industry CO₂ since 1750, to 2024: USA 435, China 285, Russia 123, Germany 95, UK 80 billion tonnes, of a world total of 1,849 (23.5%, 15.4%, 6.6%, 5.1%, 4.3%); the UK held 99% of the total in 1800 and 78% in 1850; the US total passed the UK''s in 1911'
    - id: owid_annual
      title: Annual CO₂ emissions
      authors: Our World in Data, from the Global Carbon Budget (2025)
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/annual-co2-emissions-per-country
      finding: in 2024 China emitted 12.3 billion tonnes and the US 4.9 billion

    cards rank cites ["owid_cum"] size 2 ends ["most","least"] hidden true
        * "USA" icon.of "flag united states" icon.set twemoji
        * "China" icon.of "flag china" icon.set twemoji
        * "Russia" icon.of "flag russia" icon.set twemoji
        * "GER" icon.of "flag germany" icon.set twemoji
        * "UK" icon.of "flag united kingdom" icon.set twemoji
    text yesterday "per year: China ×2.5 USA" #2f6b8f cites ["owid_annual"] x 420 y 600 font_size 42 hidden true
    text y2024 "by 2024" #5e584e x 330 y 500 font_size 60 hidden true
    text y1850 "by 1850" #b5482e x 560 y 560 font_size 60 hidden true
    text us1911 "1911: passed UK ↘" #2f6b8f cites ["owid_cum"] x 700 y 300 font_size 40 hidden true

    card title "Most CO₂ since 1750?"

A: Since 1750, which country has put the most carbon dioxide into the air? Five suspects.
    draw rank

B: That's easy. China, with all those coal plants. Britain is a tiny island, so last.
    highlight rank

    ask "Least to most, then Done." on rank store r
        right: You got {r}. America tops the list, and China is second.
        wrong: You got {r}. America comes first, then China, Russia, Germany and Britain.

    erase rank

A: Here is each country's share of all the carbon dioxide from fossil fuels so far. America alone: almost a quarter.
    draw axes bar_1 bar_2 bar_3 bar_4 bar_5 y2024

B: Hold on. China burns far more than America these days.
    draw yesterday

A: It does, about two and a half times as much a year. But it started late, so its total is about fifteen percent.
    highlight bar_4

    erase yesterday

B: Fine. And Britain, four percent. Told you: nothing to see there.
    highlight bar_1

    erase y2024

    draw y1850

A: Now wind the clock back to 1850. By then, Britain had made almost four fifths of all the carbon dioxide ever.
    animate stage 1 duration 2.5

A: And in 1800, nearly all the carbon dioxide on record came from Britain.
    highlight bar_1

B: All of it? Oh. The steam engines, the coal mines, the mills. Britain was the industrial revolution.
    icon loco size 170 set twemoji x 820 y 470 icon_look picture of locomotive

A: Exactly. America's running total only overtook Britain's in 1911.
    draw us1911

B: So the tiny island I put last is where the whole thing started. Noted.
    highlight bar_1

